ual to zero:\n\n$$\nA+{A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342194 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5292e9e-deab-5423-81ea-859716c87e84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438502} {:answer/id #uuid "6e553caf-cc56-5f3d-be8a-245cca543780" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438503} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ab33538-7993-5acb-9468-e0e3dd4ad807" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439280} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9bbb38a-9967-5612-8d8d-b7bb86341338" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438504} {:answer/id #uuid "38526a4d-7583-5f69-ae01-76ab71dc5556" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438505}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438504} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d6d93d9-8d6f-56cf-ac99-984802318cde" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439281} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6e70b79-a9e1-5d68-a28e-f96b03f12a43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438506} {:answer/id #uuid "9e9ac29b-2109-50ad-a691-a49a7e8a0ffe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438507}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438506} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1a6caeb-050e-5490-9f4b-d0d5518bd887" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439282}] :question/id #uuid "e68d4b2f-c3b6-584c-8430-662a571e8316" :question/math-academy-id "q-74318" :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $C$ is upper triangular\n- **II.** $C$ is lower triangular\n- **III.** ${C}^{T}$ is upper triangular" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. All the entries below the main diagonal of $C$ are zeros:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, since $C$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false, since ${C}^{T}$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342195 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31f0fe91-c16f-5c88-98c3-6c20947ef352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438508} {:answer/id #uuid "e7ecd97a-ece8-52f9-9c37-9224155d587f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438508} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f499a2d-45d0-590b-973b-c8d0cb52b220" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439283} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "128b04a8-57bd-5b61-874d-aac65e3e9c51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438510} {:answer/id #uuid "a75398e2-65af-5bac-9ad1-259f5a296fa1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438511}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438511} :answer-field/id #uuid "e425ed7f-061d-59d0-bf87-86d0b218dab4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439284} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "838a0ff9-f487-5659-a60a-b8467710d4e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438512} {:answer/id #uuid "fe5b9217-4edb-562b-8962-681ef51863e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438513} :answer-field/id #uuid "716e9941-8550-5bde-a973-86bb302cfd14" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439285}] :question/id #uuid "10915988-162b-5dec-9de2-5241d5fc3202" :question/math-academy-id "q-74319" :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$D=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $D$ is upper triangular\n\n- **II.** $D$ is lower triangular\n\n- **III.** ${D}^{T}$ is upper triangular" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false, since $D$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. All the entries above the main diagonal of $D$ are zeros:\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. All the entries below the main diagonal of ${D}^{T}$ are zeros:\n\n$$\n{D}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488404 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "539855fa-6c5d-53c2-8e6b-3ae037750849" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488400} {:answer/id #uuid "88990fe2-e5bf-51c0-a552-f3a9611b1ebd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488400} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f123478-0b1d-5380-b456-3eb2029b111c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488396} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1094c3c3-975f-530e-bff0-7807d9d9ab97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488395} {:answer/id #uuid "334bed91-dadd-511d-a2e8-3228c1bd2233" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488397}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488395} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f11f16f-2bde-5b13-90cc-e018dd7a5dfc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488402} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35c1b49e-afb2-5995-9b1c-7a650c3923c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488398} {:answer/id #uuid "52d664dd-84d9-50fd-8032-ee9ee3585001" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488399} :answer-field/id #uuid "a54ab5f5-3aa4-5cb2-a67f-b05de4913639" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488403}] :question/id #uuid "ac6bf26c-daf9-5149-b82c-ecff54a2e1d7" :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -7 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $B$ is upper triangular\n- **II.** $B$ is lower triangular\n- **III.** $B-{B}^{T}$ is upper triangular" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true, since all the entries below the main diagonal equal to zero:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -7 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, since $B$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -7 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false, since the result of $B-{B}^{T}$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nB-{B}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 0 & -7 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Correct Statements About a Matrix"}] :topic/math-academy-id 1777 :topic/title "Triangular Matrices"}] [{:activity/_scope [{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120897} :activity/id #uuid "4a64e93c-7c38-5a2c-bcd0-c1efea32558e" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120897 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186121051 :tutorial/content "Any plane can be uniquely determined by a point and two non-parallel direction vectors. For example, let $\\Pi$ be the plane that passes through the point $P(1,0,2)$ and is parallel to the vectors $\\mathbf{b}= \\langle 0,3,0 \\rangle$  and $\\mathbf{c}= \\langle -1,1,1 \\rangle.$\n\n![](images/ea/ea4ce822abec2b68d2471a2787f4e045493ca43c1c6795a7e0069de80cb5adee.png)\n\nUsing the vectors $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{c},$ we can construct a **parametric equation** of the plane.\n\nFirst, let $R$ be any general point in the plane, with position vector $\\mathbf{r}.$ Notice that we can get from $P$ to $R$ using a linear combination of $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{c}$ with some (unknown for us) coefficients $s$ and $t$, as shown below.\n\n![](images/b4/b40f91c3d75f092c7b29f19770364e7518d37b64ba594a311a762ad79a950e4f.png)\n\nSo, we can write the **parametric equation** of the plane as\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}\\mathbf{r}} = \\mathbf{p}+s{\\color{blue}\\,\\mathbf{b}}+t\\,{\\color{blue}\\mathbf{c}},\n\t\\qquad s,t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).\n$$\n\nThis formula works whenever $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{c}$ are not parallel.\n\nIn our case, $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{c}$ are indeed not parallel to each other. So, using column vector notation, the parametric equation for the plane $\\Pi$ is given by\n![](images/0d/0d40f8f87e1ed3f3bf5040e925e545169f5528f32cf8dd0052375aa560cc1381.svg)" :tutorial/id #uuid "2828346e-3bca-51a8-a6ef-a86ca7034a62" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3257 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "9e58d46a-ae91-5ee2-88e7-83dddd91cd81" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120898}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120898 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119933 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b02f02f1-f270-55e0-a7a9-0b729c4d82c0"} :step/id #uuid "9f747cb6-7704-53df-bc68-9a201f538aa3" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120899}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120899 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119934 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62196ae9-df2e-5a3a-bc0a-1c0f4c40af3e"} :step/id #uuid "aa340a23-a5f7-53c0-a279-cfaa2cb34f68" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120900}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120900 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119935 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3061cb06-f57f-57c8-8821-dbd962b1e78e"} :step/id #uuid "0b7d4f28-8841-5518-ad36-74e1aa0d9163" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120901}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120901 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186121052 :tutorial/content "Any plane can be uniquely determined by three non-collinear points. \n\n![](images/08/08e65c4e3465a4bf155dfed6bc0dc2a35bf2eb9326d9bff0c0aa75b86e97d76b.png)\n\nTo write down a parametric equation of the plane, the trick is to use the three non-collinear points to construct two displacement vectors that are parallel to the plane.\n\n![](images/16/1613ea9df76b637b93e0e4b38b70b87892140398eaa7aaccb74f2a5642124dfd.png)\n\nThen we can proceed as usual to find the equation of the plane. Let's practice this technique in the following example." :tutorial/id #uuid "e32f2dc4-38f6-541d-9dc6-9cfd1ac079eb" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3258 :tutorial/title "Finding the Equation of a Plane Passing Through Three Points"} :step/id #uuid "43769a60-5b42-5a2c-82fa-0054a159b437" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120902}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120902 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119936 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d11f13f0-1cfa-59ec-a04a-9483d942b1aa"} :step/id #uuid "a2d3f79a-dc28-5d90-9d1f-404334ec9529"}] :activity/title "The Parametric Equations of a Plane" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186120017} {:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423364} :activity/id #uuid "3089dbbe-cc2f-5f60-8b4c-786b3272c8cf" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423364 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120225 :question/id #uuid "0602f3f6-acc2-53ef-a72e-b71caa5d5289"} :step/id #uuid "2f9f2ed5-353f-52bf-a2a3-853d4a9582d6" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423365}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423365 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338862 :question/id #uuid "b2e1c378-a183-516b-92fd-1753dcbc375f"} :step/id #uuid "43654397-35b1-5e26-a4f3-f83c5d045414" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423366}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423366 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338865 :question/id #uuid "63af645f-746e-5e92-b7a0