t⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-3,0,1⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $H(-3,2,7)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $h=⟨-3,2,7⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =h+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨-3,2,7⟩+s⟨-3,0,1⟩+t⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398347 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c55c069-4c02-5970-a366-2d87c0faefc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨4,4,1⟩+t⟨5,5,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398349} {:answer/id #uuid "e1c9d880-a1e1-5be5-8507-819f78ea66e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,8,11⟩+s⟨-3,4,1⟩+t⟨2,3,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398350} {:answer/id #uuid "ee62040f-08f9-5abf-8ec9-6681c3d75424" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨4,-2,1⟩+t⟨3,5,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398351} {:answer/id #uuid "fd9a749a-2d90-567b-9b9e-9eea1e14d989" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨-2,4,1⟩+t⟨2,5,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398352} {:answer/id #uuid "3fbcf038-f3dc-5a71-b0c2-b0f15532c018" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,5,11⟩+s⟨2,4,1⟩+t⟨2,3,-5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398353}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨-2,4,1⟩+t⟨2,5,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398352} :answer-field/id #uuid "f112cd0f-0678-5784-90d3-7e1ee7077df9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398348}] :question/id #uuid "0fce542a-476c-5ad1-ad5a-b30b8a4bb006" :question/math-academy-id "q-128499" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $B(1,5,13)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨-7,12,5⟩+s⟨-2,4,1⟩$ and $r=⟨-9,21,2⟩+t⟨2,5,-3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-2,4,1⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨2,5,-3⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $B(1,5,13)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $b=⟨1,5,13⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =b+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨-2,4,1⟩+t⟨2,5,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Lines"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119936 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119649 :question/id #uuid "9c36ddd5-fcf1-5c4d-a350-aa8ef3a3ca9e" :question/math-academy-id "e-4942" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $A(-1,4,-3),$ $B(7,5,4),$ and $C(2,-2,8).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨7,5,4⟩-⟨-1,4,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,1,7⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =⟨2,-2,8⟩-⟨-1,4,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-6,11⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle -1,4,-3 \\rangle$ of the point $A,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =a+s\\overset{\\to }{AB}+t\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\ r & =⟨-1,4,-3⟩+s⟨8,1,7⟩+t⟨3,-6,11⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Watch out!** The form of the final equation depends on our choice of vectors and the point on the plane. We could have picked other vectors. Likewise, we could have chosen $B$ or $C$ instead of $A$ as our point on the plane. So, the answer is *not unique*!"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d11f13f0-1cfa-59ec-a04a-9483d942b1aa" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120218 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b98d4014-27ab-5ffc-a9a1-94f2d76d7cfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = ⟨3, 1, 5⟩ + s⟨3,-9,-5⟩ + t⟨ - 2, 1, 3⟩, s, t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117470} {:answer/id #uuid "cfe44dd9-7bdd-5239-bc90-bb3f3d5c8dd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117471} {:answer/id #uuid "d9d68798-b39f-5fd9-ad83-ef58d2f0912b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = ⟨3, 1, 5⟩ + s⟨3,-9,-5⟩ + t⟨ - 5, 0,-2⟩, s, t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117472} {:answer/id #uuid "fd46fa5e-f228-5b17-ab87-937c2c49b057" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = ⟨3, 1, 5⟩ + s⟨6,-8, 0⟩ + t⟨ - 2, 1, 3⟩, s, t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117473} {:answer/id #uuid "164382bd-289b-5666-97e1-536a448ecc74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = ⟨3, 1, 5⟩ + s⟨6,-8, 0⟩ + t⟨ - 5, 0,-2⟩, s, t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117474}] :answer-field/id #uuid "b6cca1ea-c183-5baf-841b-897aa164800b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117469} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a00e2b8e-5c43-5f1e-861a-b8621cd03fb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390836} {:answer/id #uuid "d0576584-3750-547a-9169-cba885383592" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,1,5⟩+s⟨3,-9,-5⟩+t⟨-2,1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390837} {:answer/id #uuid "cc58ca2d-f965-5a26-a6a7-4b5c5d9d1c6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,1,5⟩+s⟨6,-8,0⟩+t⟨-5,0,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390838} {:answer/id #uuid "448cf521-8dea-57c9-a228-ac326b781ae6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,1,5⟩+s⟨3,-9,-5⟩+t⟨-5,0,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390839} {:answer/id #uuid "e6fdd784-d294-5584-81fc-4a5e521dbe8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,1,5⟩+s⟨6,-8,0⟩+t⟨-2,1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,1,5⟩+s⟨3,-9,-5⟩+t⟨-5,0,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390839} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f59cecd-7538-5379-bf6c-ff75d0435b9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390835}] :question/id #uuid "26d7019c-08c2-5f92-a7e5-2893b8366abc" :question/math-academy-id "q-32988" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $A(3,1,5),\\,B(6,-8,0)$, and $C(-2,1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨6,-8,0⟩-⟨3,1,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-9,-5⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =⟨-2,1,3⟩-⟨3,1,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,0,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $a=⟨3,1,5⟩$ of the point $A,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =a+s\\overset{\\to }{AB}+t\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\ r & =⟨3,1,5⟩+s⟨3,-9,-5⟩+t⟨-5,0,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120219 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #u