envector ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1-5\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$*" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 26 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nWe are given the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=5\\text{i}$ and the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1-5\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}$ is \n${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}.$ But we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=5\\text{i}$ and its associated eigenvector is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1-5\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{5\\text{i}t}.\n$$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1-5\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{5\\text{i}t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1-5\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)-5\\text{i}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t))+\\text{i}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix}+\\text{i}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+\\text{i}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(0) & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1}-5{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & =1\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix}+0\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391373 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e932bf7-b9db-535d-b1d7-2c47f0a471ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391375} {:answer/id #uuid "57f72f11-38e7-5f9a-8e91-eba04c0da69c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-13\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391376} {:answer/id #uuid "336353e