C.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{C}.$ First, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375096 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "885275fa-0273-572d-b4ee-cd12300d505e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 7 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375098} {:answer/id #uuid "132ab69d-5679-5d1c-a1bc-aa2c6fcdc223" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375099} {:answer/id #uuid "a56f3d7b-6da1-52d8-acb8-91f8eaa8c91d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375100} {:answer/id #uuid "1bfad28a-987c-5e44-ae2b-d9da6d1bae04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375101} {:answer/id #uuid "86726a21-1a03-57e3-a79b-8a0905cbc6ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375102}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 7 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375098} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ba2eb2d-11d8-5382-b28d-dd3142a80d57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375097}] :question/id #uuid "171fe4ce-730c-5fbe-99a6-2dbc5de82526" :question/math-academy-id "q-38357" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{P}_{C\\to B}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $[T]_{C}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $C$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $B.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/2e/2e82c232614bec8a98f079ea56d7913ee13e7b457e33e418198278d2e369fc5c.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}.\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{B}.$ Solving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-2)\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 3}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 7 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388702 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39af9a4f-5bb0-5f67-b99e-b356fdeef13f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}20 & -36 \\\\ 14 & -25\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388704} {:answer/id #uuid "24019f33-d58e-5c2e-9bc0-2466a9447e60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}20 & 36 \\\\ -25 & 14\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388705} {:answer/id #uuid "9eb9cc07-a4ed-5da6-b193-1c9894ee42b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}14 & -25 \\\\ 20 & -36\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388706} {:answer/id #uuid "1667976f-4e72-5f00-aab0-1b8c12345f8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}14 & -36 \\\\ 20 & -25\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388707} {:answer/id #uuid "d77416b1-f86b-5a81-a593-653abb91c3eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}25 & -36 \\\\ 14 & -20\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}20 & -36 \\\\ 14 & -25\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388704} :answer-field/id #uuid "6811151d-cd95-5e12-aa34-9045fdbee48f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388703}] :question/id #uuid "3fe32d4d-9284-57a0-89e5-58bdfd98337d" :question/math-academy-id "q-140454" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{P}_{B\\to C}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $B$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to C}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{C}.$ First, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 5}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}20 & -36 \\\\ 14 & -25\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395222 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2c5ed32-df5f-5079-9d02-d5c9ada85034" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -16 \\\\ 4 & 11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395224} {:answer/id #uuid "baecf3f2-1d2c-5db8-85e1-ee333fed3cf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395225} {:answer/id #uuid "cb0787be-7b6f-5bb6-82b7-843413949641" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395226} {:answer/id #uuid "c0d06cf4-5d42-5235-9522-379af5716752" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -8 \\\\ -4 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395227} {:answer/id #uuid "ff4cd99a-0ee7-58a2-9df9-8077ce6f8c87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}14 & -20 \\\\ -12 & 17\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395226} :answer-field/id #uuid "ceaa3e2d-722d-5f73-8fd9-98a8664a5416" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395223}] :question/id #uuid "c8232ae8-3dbc-5fa7-a890-a6276b10aff3" :question/math-academy-id "q-97114" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{P}_{C\\to B}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $[T]_{C}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $C$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $B.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/2e/2e82c232614bec8a98f079ea56d7913ee13e7b457e33e418198278d2e369fc5c.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}.\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{B}.$ Solving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} & ={\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 3-2\\cdot 4}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 11\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395229 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0609b365-00a9-5e3f-b18a-4ae8f0cb6423" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 7 \\\\ -6 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395231} {:answer/id #uuid "900a056b-ff09-5fb7-93ec-d70236eeac1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395232} {:answer/id #uuid "5e60741c-2d26-5cbb-b653-d42461c6724c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395233} {:answer/id #uuid "a567a6a7-4ff1-59da-a544-576e1192accc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 9 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395234} {:answer/id #uuid "c2fc3385-8e0c-58d4-8ac0-fc0beafee826" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -1 \\\\ -8 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395235}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395232} :answer-field/id #uuid "161f0cc1-c732-5e8a-bdbf-03f067c9d5be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395230}] :question/id #uuid "65dae103-c225-5d3f-8973-42e2dd0c3a80" :question/math-academy-id "q-97115" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{C}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,{P}_{C\\to B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $[T]_{C}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $C$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $B.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/2e/2e82c232614bec8a98f079ea56d7913ee13e7b457e33e418198278d2e369fc5c.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}.\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{B}.$ Solving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-1)\\cdot (-5)-3\\cdot 2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395236 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bd7cba7-4aea-5bfa-ac53-5e6bfef17303" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395238} {:answer/id #uuid "0e9f165b-892b-54a7-ac32-c6ee54ed56fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 9 \\\\ -2 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395239} {:answer/id #uuid "74ebb876-d1f9-5de2-836d-0ce54e1671e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 & -5 \\\\ 26 & -11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395240} {:answer/id #uuid "4d9b8101-9235-5bd1-9d67-397ac4faea30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395241} {:answer/id #uuid "c4818d98-198b-548b-8121-0a8b48614740" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}10 & -7 \\\\ 24 & -17\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395242}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 9 \\\\ -2 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395239} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd97dd2b-5eec-58d6-9066-ccafa818ca4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395237}] :question/id #uuid "4f59fe0b-284b-5212-bd9c-6b6ffbb22f39" :question/math-academy-id "q-97116" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{P}_{B\\to C}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $B$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to C}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{C}.$ First, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 5-(-2)\\cdot (-2)}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 9 \\\\ -2 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419683 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cd07fe6-6fc8-5bf5-a02a-2d9be90b12af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 6 \\\\ -14 & -10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419666} {:answer/id #uuid "5e5ddfaa-301e-59f4-a460-764955ae24fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 6 \\\\ -14 & -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419668} {:answer/id #uuid "6431b