ix}-8 & 5 \\\\ 39 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269907} {:answer/id #uuid "4d2b8368-af12-5270-8abb-2966b96811f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 39 \\\\ 8 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269962} {:answer/id #uuid "52a4f459-56be-5d2b-aa62-980c1e97fec0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-39 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270004}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -39 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269595} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f4347d9-b9dd-5363-a53a-02a14e4ccbbc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271532}] :question/id #uuid "ac66a375-3ba5-552a-83b4-35e3ded13468" :question/math-academy-id "q-140482" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\},\\,[T]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to this basis. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the basis $B$ and standard basis $S$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/db/dbd020362f950fe8bfb4c592652b9e78a73610fa01a247b0b7ead6f201bf9ea5.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{S}={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1},\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} & ={\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 5}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{S} & ={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -39 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360754 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "182077b4-5f2c-531e-96ce-4b88e8ab4d4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 10 \\\\ -5 & 13\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357964} {:answer/id #uuid "42fae3bb-9ef9-579c-b81a-3be55f9c0d12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 16 \\\\ -11 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358324} {:answer/id #uuid "6ec1f99a-0977-5b71-97c0-662f0436dfd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 8 \\\\ -9 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358716} {:answer/id #uuid "be23d718-4726-5599-970d-363a78d2bd57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359411} {:answer/id #uuid "de1c3f3a-b06a-5be2-a7ff-4c20229cd2ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359703}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359411} :answer-field/id #uuid "215bd893-15dc-5185-8467-98be175ac074" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360051}] :question/id #uuid "143b7701-47b4-58ee-98d5-de35b377edb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-97119" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\},\\,[T]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to this basis. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the basis $B$ and standard basis $S$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/db/dbd020362f950fe8bfb4c592652b9e78a73610fa01a247b0b7ead6f201bf9ea5.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{S}={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1},\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot (-3)-(-1)\\cdot 2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{S} & ={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360755 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04ab380b-359f-5fa7-9dd1-5f1f687f5511" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}11 & 7 \\\\ 8 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357796} {:answer/id #uuid "155b0ef5-ee12-5bbc-9dcb-79ae79e2a845" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357940} {:answer/id #uuid "2598bd34-3569-5f50-a023-f6c6e289174b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}17 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358090} {:answer/id #uuid "c0e07147-0972-5a53-bf9f-6b81b9f73133" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359442} {:answer/id #uuid "e3f66fb5-a4f6-5e6e-aa7e-7e4c763c1153" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -9 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359442} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f593899-661f-517f-adb3-211823b247d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360025}] :question/id #uuid "18ca38eb-405c-519d-860c-9cd4de1b59e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-97120" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\},\\,[T]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to this basis. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the basis $B$ and standard basis $S$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/db/dbd020362f950fe8bfb4c592652b9e78a73610fa01a247b0b7ead6f201bf9ea5.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{S}={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1},\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 6}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{S} & ={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360756 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b475445-5cb4-5710-982b-724fa1edd22e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ -23 & 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358141} {:answer/id #uuid "66790505-e184-5aa7-b181-1d0f53118c51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 23 & -10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358648} {:answer/id #uuid "81f4c14a-f6f2-5e02-b601-4575f31e25cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 \\\\ 23 & -10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358888} {:answer/id #uuid "adafbfb4-cdbb-5b64-803a-bfb001366afb" :answer/type {:db/ident :a