my-id "q-97064" :question/problem "Let $[T]_{B}$ and $[T]_{C}$ be the matrices of a linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C,$ respectively. If ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from basis $C$ to basis $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}$\n- **II.** $[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}$\n- **III.** $[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/9b/9ba3d1f0eebdfc82c40f36bdbe16896ca15516b623c695b72c331861955329bc.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360749 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "adfa5bb0-95dd-5e0f-a753-c9aa882957ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452299} {:answer/id #uuid "42f83495-bf79-5e40-bb79-ee3727fa8353" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452299} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0a51104-0991-584c-8840-d4699e193686" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452997} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc60e