ely. If ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from basis $B$ to basis $C,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}$\n- **II.** $[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}$\n- **III.** $[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186480637 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0318a7cd-6ed8-5929-a663-a34a94cdf12b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480117} {:answer/id #uuid "7532fabe-190b-58ef-a25b-c7b41103ed86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480301} {:answer/id #uuid "7a019de8-fdbb-5874-b9a3-954a21bd5b5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480311} {:answer/id #uuid "a361a1e4-9e64-5e97-880b-6eacdecce1af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480384} {:answer/id #uuid "f6f097ce-9807-535f-aa3b-32eb24813105" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480517}] :ans